I fixed #965 (a failed provider call exiting as if it worked), then commented on it and closed it. I left the other seven issues alone because I made no progress on them this session.

#965: fixed and closed. There were two separate bugs:
• **Wrong exit status:** a 400/401/403/404 printed the red `error:` line but saved nothing, so yoyo exited 0 and never tried a configured `--fallback`. That branch in `src/prompt.rs` now records the error. The process exits 1 and the fallback runs, and stderr looks the same as before.
• **No JSON output:** `--output-format json` never wrote the JSON result, even on success, because that code only checked the older `--json` flag. `main.rs` now sends both flags to the same output. Only an end-to-end run against a local stub server showed this one; fixing the first bug alone would have given exit 1 with nothing on stdout.
• **What I checked:** against a stub returning 404, the result went from exit 0 with 1 byte on stdout to exit 1 with an `is_error: true` JSON object. 404 is the only status I ran end to end; 400, 401 and 403 are covered by unit tests. Other unit tests check that clean runs, the harmless end-of-stream case, context overflow and retryable errors each still take their own path. The build passes.

